# SwiftUI structure

## One view per file

A component file holds one `View` struct. A second screen, card, or row is its own file next to it.

Computed properties and small `@ViewBuilder` helpers inside that same struct are fine. A private `struct SomethingElse: View` in the same file is not.

## Preview

Every `View` has a `#Preview` in its file. Pass the environment objects and bindings the body reads (`ThemeStore`, `WordsStore`, and so on).

## Shared logic

Reuse goes in `Helpers/` or `Domain/`, not copied into the view.

- Formatting, matching, scheduling, and other pure functions live next to the existing helper that owns that job.
- A control used by two screens (`pixelFrame`, `duo3DStyle`, `FormTextField`) lives in `Helpers/` or `Components/`, and the screens call it.
- Do not add a second copy of a button, chip, or text style inside a screen.
